      "repair": "No prompt change needed; flag for compiler to ensure only explicit reaction rows (not text-embedded emoji) are used when constructing match/negative reaction facts."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "The design correctly implements the route USER→REACTION→MESSAGE→CONVERSATION→WORKSPACE: reactor_priya and reactor_kenji are genuine rocket reactions on messages actually located in the two named channels (verified against base_seed messages 1706067472 in C_INFRA and 1706028229 in C_GROWTH), giving a valid 'multiple' resolution. Negatives are well-differentiated: wrong-channel-right-emoji (Mateo in frontend, Robert in model-research), right-channel-wrong-emoji (Sophie's thumbsup), and authorship-without-reaction (Łukasz) — all faithfully representing distinct failure modes tied to real relationship edges rather than table-name conflation. Channel/workspace scoping is achievable through conversations.list (public channels) plus conversations.history and reactions.get, consistent with documented API capabilities and without requiring unavailable workspace-name enumeration. Answer attributes are legitimate bare user columns. The only concerns are stylistic/quality-level: the prompt's DM-sending motivation isn't reflected as an actual action in the obligations (making this essentially a bare retrieval task), and embedded 🚀 characters in unrelated message text create a minor risk of confusion during compilation, though not a structural defect."
